de", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 151-156", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "modelling_pipeline_config_exclude_regions", "label": "exclude_regions spatial filter", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 57-64", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "modelling_pipeline_config_log_transform_target", "label": "log_transform_target", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "line 53", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "modelling_pipeline_config_do_shap_refined_tuning", "label": "do_shap_refined_tuning (Step 3 re-tune toggle)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "line 42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_robust_multiseed_evaluation", "label": "Robust multiseed CV evaluation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 18, 100-103, 279", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reported performance depends on fold construction and seed; running tuning, SHAP pruning and evaluation across multiple fold seeds reduces split-variance artifacts. Evaluation uses a disjoint eval_fold_seed_list and outputs are written to a run-scoped folder named from the robust seeds."}, {"id": "readme_run_scoped_output_folder", "label": "Run-scoped output folder output/pixel_grouped_<seeds>/", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 27, 94, 135-139", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Folder name is derived from robust_fold_seed_list (hyphen-separated) so each multiseed run's selection, tuning, evaluation, diagnostics and _run_metadata/pipeline_config_effective.rds are isolated and reproducible; multiseed_run_output_id is retained only for compatibility."}, {"id": "readme_output_cache", "label": "output/cache/ shared cache (folds, prediction grids)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 173-181, 200", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cached fold .rds and prediction_grid_cache_*.rds files are shared across runs to speed re-runs; deleting a cache file forces recomputation."}, {"id": "readme_all_extracted_new_dataset", "label": "data/all_extracted_new.rds (main extracted dataset)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 52, 99, 120", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_final_models", "label": "output/<cv_regime>/final_models/*_final.rds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 106, 143, 169", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_random_split_cv", "label": "random_split CV", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "line 194", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Naive row split; duplicate covariates leak between train and test, so results are a highly optimistic baseline."}, {"id": "readme_location_grouped_cv", "label": "location_grouped_random CV", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "line 195", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Groups rows sharing the same (longitude, latitude); prevents duplicate-coordinate leakage but not leakage from distinct locations in the same coarse raster pixel."}, {"id": "readme_pixel_grouped_cv", "label": "pixel_grouped_random CV (publication grouping)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 83, 196", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rows with identical raster-derived covariate vectors share a fold, so the model is never evaluated on inputs seen verbatim in training (common at ~4 km resolution). Strictly more conservative than location grouping; chosen as primary strategy for tuning, pruning and importance and reported in the paper."}, {"id": "readme_spatial_block_cv", "label": "spatial_block_<m>m CV", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 83-85, 156, 197, 278", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Holds out whole spatial blocks to test extrapolation to new geography; not recommended as the main regime because of existing spatial clustering and a small dataset. Workflow is designed for gap-filling near sampled conditions, and spatial CV shows degradation when extrapolating."}, {"id": "readme_region_stratified_cv", "label": "region_stratified_<m>m CV", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "line 198", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Spatial blocks built within each ecoregion and folds combined so each fold keeps multi-region representation, reducing leave-one-region-out artifacts."}, {"id": "readme_covariate_pruning", "label": "Covariate pruning / variable selection (correlation filter + permutation + SHAP)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 66-73, 188", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Correlation filter (|r| > 0.8) drops redundant covariates before per-model permutation importance (n_permutations default 1 because expensive; permutation_max_vars 15; feature_coverage 0.99) and optional SHAP selection (use_shap_per_model TRUE). Per-model sets are written to pruned_model_variables_perm.csv / pruned_model_variables_shap.csv."}, {"id": "readme_shap_pruning", "label": "Robust SHAP pruning (Step 2)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 42, 101-102", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_gaussian_process_regressor", "label": "Gaussian Process Regressor (GPR)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 3, 77, 217-231", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_generalised_additive_model", "label": "Generalised Additive Model (GAM)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 3, 77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_xgboost", "label": "XGBoost regressor (XGB)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 3, 77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_linear_regressor", "label": "Linear Regressor (LR)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 3, 77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "predict_gpr_at_points", "label": "predict_gpr_at_points.R", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 217-231", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "predict_gpr_at_points_ipynb", "label": "predict_gpr_at_points.ipynb (R kernel notebook)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 220-224", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Notebook sources the R script so prediction logic and editable paths stay in one place."}, {"id": "prediction_maps_ipynb", "label": "prediction_maps.ipynb (Python carbon stock maps)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 214, 233-242", "source_u